    "result_text": "The full suite consists of the single `AcceptanceTest`, and it passes. The change is complete and green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe API now returns a `timezone` field on owners, derived from the locality region via the fixed table (NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney, VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne, QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane).\n\nChanges, each kept in its proper place:\n\n- **`model/RegionTimezone.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, single-responsibility lookup class holding the fixed region\u2192IANA-timezone table, mirroring the existing `RegionPostcodes`/`Locality` model classes. Returns `null` for a null or unknown region.\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `timezone` mapping backed by a new `formatTimezone(owner)` helper that **reuses** the existing `formatLocality(owner)` to obtain the region, then delegates to `RegionTimezone.forRegion(...)`. No table logic is duplicated.\n- **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared the read-only `timezone` property on the owner schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\nThe acceptance test (`locality` = NSW, `timezone` = Australia/Sydney for a Sydney owner) passes; `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
